ble name to logs (as in "log_path.exe_name.pid").\x00' 0x2a0@0x15507|0x15498=b'log_suffix\x00' 0x2a4@0x183bf|0x1831f=b'String to append to log file name, e.g. ".txt".\x00' 0x2d4@0x11060|0x11058=b'log_to_syslog\x00' 0x2d8@0x17a8e|0x179ee=b'Write all sanitizer output to syslog in addition to other means of logging.\x00' 0x308@0x114fe|0x114f6=b'verbosity\x00' 0x30c@0x1e394|0x1e286=b'Verbosity level (0 - silent, 1 - a bit of output, 2+ - more output).\x00' 0x33c@0x19254|0x191c4=b'strip_env\x00' 0x340@0x12899|0x12887=b'Whether to remove the sanitizer from DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES to avoid passing it to children on Apple platforms. Default is true.\x00' 0x370@0x141f4|0x141bd=b'verify_interceptors\x00' 0x374@0x12919|0x12907=b'Verify that interceptors are working on Apple platforms. Default is true.\x00' 0x3a4@0x17ada|0x17a3a=b'detect_leaks\x00' 0x3a8@0x17ae7|0x17a47=b'Enable memory leak detection.\x00' 0x3d8@0x14cd0|0x14c99=b'leak_check_at_exit\x00' 0x3dc@0x14208|0x141d1=b'Invoke leak checking in an atexit handler. Has no effect if detect_leaks=false, or if __lsan_do_leak_check() is called before the handler has a chance to run.\x00' 0x40c@0x16faa|0x16f32=b'allocator_may_return_null\x00' 0x410@0x12197|0x1218f=b'If false, the allocator will crash instead of returning 0 on out-of-memory.\x00' 0x440@0x1d548|0x1d447=b'print_summary\x00' 0x444@0x142a7|0x14270=b'If false, disable printing error summaries in addition to error reports.\x00' 0x474@0x13acb|0x13a94=b'print_module_map\x00' 0x478@0x1c519|0x1c42f=b"Print the process module map where supported (0 - don't print, 1 - print only once before process exits, 2 - print after each report).\x00" 0x4a8@0x1e3d9|0x1e2cb=b'check_printf\x00' 0x4ac@0x1cca6|0x1cbb4=b'Check printf arguments.\x00' 0x4e4@0x16c10|0x16b98=b'handle_segv\x00' 0x4e8@0x1ed12|0x1ec04=b"Controls custom tool's SIGSEGV handler (0 - do not registers the handler, 1 - register the handler and allow user to set own, 2 - registers the handler and block user from changing it